  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#46705\", \"PowerToys#47966\"], \"answer\": \"This request has been filed before. Ticket PowerToys#46705 (\\\"Dock: Add support for a band in the taskbar too\\\") contains the same text and screenshots, copied in from this ticket's author ([user], in #50930). In that ticket the maintainer said a taskbar band for the Command Palette Dock is on the roadmap. There is a prototype branch, but it still has edge cases to fix. Those include centered taskbars, display changes, Windows 10, vertical taskbars, and the Widgets button. There is no release date, so follow that ticket and add your use case there. For media controls now, PowerToys#47966 was closed. The maintainers recommend the community extension 'MediaControlsExtension' by [user] for Command Palette. It shows a dock band with the current track and play, pause and skip buttons. It hides when nothing is playing. A first-party media extension is not planned. Volume mixer and EQ features are not covered in either ticket.\"}",
